		{
			description: [
				"The Virtual Space Manager is a massive computer oriented program that normally results in special knowledge only."
				""
				"However, the mass-energy boundary is so thin and computing knowledge so wide that we can now \"virtualize\" normal interactions and have those interactions happen to an object."
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"The cost to maintain the virtualization per tick is 1 eu/block/(vtick/s)/TempK. "
				""
				"That might seem like a nice and cheap number, but to virtualize a block size of 16x16x16 at 20 vticks per second at Cosmic Background Radiation (3K) is already 245760 eu to maintain, or nearly 2 ZPM amps per tick!"
				""
				"Fortunately, I have upgrades that you can use to your advantage."
				""
				"Remember that upgrade colors correlates to typing and RGB can be arranged in a circle clockwise, so the clockwise type to R is G."
				""
				"Temperature => Red"
				"Time => Green"
				"Space => Blue"
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				""
				"Note that the Virtual Space Manager only considers temperature in its average form."
				""
				"If an event causes an expansion, the space will automatically adjust and proceed to eat more of your energy budget."
				"If an event causes an increase in heat, temperature costs will continue to rise."
				""
				"If the VSM fails with the temperature above 3,000 K, it explode GT5 Nuclear Style."
				""
				"If the VSM fails with tick speed above 30 vticks, the VSM becomes contaminated with \"unstable chronoparticles\". Having an \"infected\" block/item in your inventory gives you \"time warp\", which is just blindness, slowness, and mining fatigue. You can deal with this by having a suit with enchantment or aspect (chronoimmune)."
			]
			id: "5B4C4F7919DF9DC4"
			tasks: [{
				id: "2F852A933F1BC4D4"
				title: "Virtual Space Manager"
				type: "checkmark"
			}]
			x: -3.5d
			y: 2.0d
		}
		{
			description: [
